  "audit_findings": {
    "score_explanation": "The initial 100% accuracy was caused by target leakage in dataset construction. Class 0 URLs were bare domains without schemes or paths (num_subdirs == 0 for 100% of Class 0, and tld == NaN for 100% of Class 0 due to urlparse.netloc failure on bare domains). Class 1 URLs were full URLs with schemes and paths. Naive models split on num_subdirs and tld_Unknown to achieve artificial 100% scores. In production, PhishGuard AI pairs ML predictions with robust rule-based heuristics and threat intelligence to prevent false positives."
